// The `Send` and `Sync` markers (spec/shared.md, SH4).
//
// Neither has a method. The compiler derives them from what a type is made of: a value is `Send` when every part of it
// is, and `Sync` likewise. A type that holds a raw pointer, or a type whose safety rests on something the compiler cannot
// see (a lock, an atomic), declares them itself with an `unsafe` impl block. `task.spawn`, `thread.spawn`, `Scope.spawn`,
// `Channel`, and `Shared` ask for them.

/// A type whose values may move to another task or thread.
///
/// ```
/// fn send_to_task<T: Send>(own value: T): T {
///     value
/// }
/// assert_eq(send_to_task(String.from("moved")), String.from("moved"))
/// ```
interface Send { }

/// A type that several tasks or threads may use at once through shared views (`&T`).
///
/// ```
/// fn share<T: Sync>(own value: T): T {
///     value
/// }
/// assert_eq(share(5), 5)
/// ```
interface Sync { }
